ts */\r\n.taptap-widgets-wrapper .widget,\r\n.taptap-widgets-wrapper .widget a {\r\n    color:;\r\n    font-size:px;\r\n    letter-spacing:px;\r\n    line-height:px;\r\n}\r\n.taptap-widgets-wrapper .widget a {\r\n    color:;\r\n}\r\n/* widget font */\r\n    \r\n/* STYLED SCROLLBAR */\r\n/* show scrollbar styling, if scrollbar enabled */\r\n\r\n/* MISC */\r\n/* show header + search when menu open */\r\n/* push down site by height of menu */\r\n/* if submenu arrow divider is hidden */\r\n/* hide taptap between resolutions */\r\n@media ( min-width:920px) and (max-width:99999px) {\r\n    .taptap-menu-button-wrapper,\r\n    .taptap-logo-wrapper,\r\n    .taptap-header,\r\n    .taptap-background-color,\r\n    .taptap-background-image,\r\n    .taptap-background-overlay,\r\n    .taptap-main-wrapper,\r\n    .taptap-search-wrapper,\r\n    .taptap-search-button-wrapper { display:none; }\r\n    html { margin-top:0 !important; }\r\n}\r\n/* hide theme menu */\r\n@media screen and (max-width:920px) {\r\n    .header-wrap { display:none !important; }\r\n}\r\n@media screen and (min-width:99999px) {\r\n    .header-wrap { display:none !important; }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<!-- END CUSTOM COLORS (WP THEME CUSTOMIZER) --><meta name=\"generator\" content=\"Powered by Visual Composer Website Builder - fast and easy-to-use drag and drop visual editor for WordPress.\"/><noscript><style>.vce-row-container .vcv-lozad {display: none}</style></noscript><script>document.documentElement.className += \" js\";</script>\r\n\n\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\" class=\"saswp-schema-markup-output\">\n[{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\\/\",\"@graph\":[{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\\/\",\"@type\":\"SiteNavigationElement\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/#sintiuis\",\"name\":\"S\\u00ednti\\u00fais\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/ga\\/sponsorship\\/\"},{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\\/\",\"@type\":\"SiteNavigationElement\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/#cad-ata-ar-siul\",\"name\":\"Cad at\\u00e1 ar si\\u00fal\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/ga\\/cad-ata-ar-siul\\/\"},{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\\/\",\"@type\":\"SiteNavigationElement\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/#oideachas\",\"name\":\"Oideachas\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/ga\\/oideachas\\/\"},{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\\/\",\"@type\":\"SiteNavigationElement\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/#leabharlann\",\"name\":\"Leabharlann\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/ga\\/leabharlann\\/\"},{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\\/\",\"@type\":\"SiteNavigationElement\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/#pobal\",\"name\":\"Pobal\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/ga\\/pobal\\/\"}]},\n\n{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\\/\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/#breadcrumb\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"item\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\",\"name\":\"Irish Cultural Centre\"}},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"item\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/\",\"name\":\"What's On | Upcoming Events - Irish Cultural Centre\"}}]},\n\n{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\\/\",\"@type\":\"MusicEvent\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/#event\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/\",\"name\":\"What&#039;s on\",\"description\":\"Contemporary Irish and London based Music Join us for a night of electrifying new music from Hawke The Band, Oscar Blue and Scarlet!\",\"location\":[[],{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Irish Cultural Centre, Hammersmith Ltd\",\"address\":{\"streetAddress\":\"5 Black\\u2019s Road\",\"postalCode\":\"W6 9DT\",\"addressCountry\":\"GB\"}}],\"eventStatus\":\"EventScheduled\",\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\"startDate\":\"2023-04-13T19:30:00-22:00\",\"endDate\":\"2023-04-13T19:30:00-22:00\",\"image\":[],\"performer\":{\"name\":\"Hawke The Band, Oscar Blue & Scarlet\"},\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"AggregateOffer\",\"highPrice\":\"7.50\",\"lowPrice\":\"5.00\",\"priceCurrency\":\"GBP\",\"availability\":\"InStock\",\"validFrom\":\"2021-05-27T13:27:31+00:00\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/\"},\"organizer\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Irish Cultural Centre\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\",\"email\":\"info@irishculturalcentre.co.uk\",\"telephone\":\"+44 2085638232\"}},\n\n{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\\/\",\"@type\":\"ExhibitionEvent\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/#event\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/\",\"name\":\"What&#039;s on\",\"description\":\"Earlier this year we collaborated with the National Army Museum on The History of Irish Regiments in the British Army. We are delighted to have in the centre for a limited time only, a focused 14 side pop up exhibition entitled \\u201cHarp and Crown\\u201d which depicts many historical accounts and the history of the Royal Irish Regiment. For information and detailed historical accounts you can also check out: https:\\/\\/www.nam.ac.uk\\/subjects\\/ireland Exhibition Location: The Mezzanine, Irish Cultural Centre Hammersmith\",\"location\":[[],{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Irish Cultural Centre, Hammersmith Ltd\",\"address\":{\"streetAddress\":\"5 Black\\u2019s Road\",\"postalCode\":\"W6 9DT\",\"addressCountry\":\"GB\"}}],\"eventStatus\":\"EventScheduled\",\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\"startDate\":\"2023-01-17T09:00:00-17:00\",\"endDate\":\"2023-01-31T09:00:00-17:00\",\"image\":[],\"performer\":{\"name\":\"National Army Museum\"},\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"AggregateOffer\",\"highPrice\":\"0.00\",\"lowPrice\":\"0.00\",\"priceCurrency\":\"GBP\",\"availability\":\"InStock\",\"validFrom\":\"2021-05-27T13:27:31+00:00\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/\"},\"organizer\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Irish Cultural Centre\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\",\"email\":\"info@irishculturalcentre.co.uk\",\"telephone\":\"+44 2085638232\"}},\n\n{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\\/\",\"@type\":\"ScreeningEvent\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/#event\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/\",\"name\":\"What&#039;s on\",\"description\":\"Followed by a Q&A with Composer Stano and Producer Denise Dunphy Hot Press says:\\u00a0\\u201c\\u2026\\u2026Lyrically and philosophically, if Sam Beckett was around today, I\\u2019d say he\\u2019d fancy a spell in the studio doing spoken word with Stano..\\u201d STANO, the groundbreaking Irish composer and electronic experimentalist,\\u00a0true to the motto of his punk roots to \\u201cbe original\\u201d, now, following screenings all over Dublin, Ireland and New York, finally brings his \\u2018Masterpiece of Storytelling\\u2019 to London In Between Silence, where we really exist is a collection of intimate personal stories by leading Irish writers and artists including Roddy Doyle, Paula Meehan, Dermot Bolger, Anne Enright, Aidan Gillen, Theo Dorgan and all who have a story to tell, presented in a unique film format by groundbreaking Irish composer STANO. STANO creates a piece of music for each participant. He doesn\\u2019t hear the story and the participant doesn\\u2019t hear the music until they start to record. His desire is to capture the spontaneous response of each person to the music and the impact it has on their delivery. STANO\\u2019s interest is in rediscovering the power of the shared experience of music and storytelling, of listening, of allowing our imagination to bring us on our own journey while engaging with the voice of the storyteller. In Between Silence, where we really exist launched at the International Literature Festival Dublin and made its North American debut with a three week run in the Barrow Street Theatre NYC. This ongoing collection of now over 100 stories, has since played at festivals throughout Ireland, New York and in March 2023 will be touring Australia. The collection is housed in the Boole Library, University College Cork alongside the Porcelain Book which accompanies the collection.\",\"location\":[[],{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Irish Cultural Centre, Hammersmith Ltd\",\"address\":{\"streetAddress\":\"5 Black\\u2019s Road\",\"postalCode\":\"W6 9DT\",\"addressCountry\":\"GB\"}}],\"eventStatus\":\"EventScheduled\",\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\"startDate\":\"2023-02-11T19:00:00-22:00\",\"endDate\":\"2023-02-11T19:00:00-22:00\",\"image\":[],\"performer\":{\"name\":\"Composer Stano and Producer Denise Dunphy\"},\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"AggregateOffer\",\"highPrice\":\"12.00\",\"lowPrice\":\"10.00\",\"priceCurrency\":\"GBP\",\"availability\":\"InStock\",\"validFrom\":\"2021-05-27T13:27:31+00:00\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/\"},\"organizer\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Irish Cultural Centre\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/irishculturalcentre.co.uk\",\"email\":\"info@irishculturalcentre.co.uk\",\"telephone\":\"+44 2085638232\"}}]\n</script>\n\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/\" crossorigin>\n<meta name=\"generator\" content=\"Powered by Slider Revolution 7.1.1 - responsive, Mobile-Friendly Slider Plugin for WordPress with comfortable drag and drop interface.\" />\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/cropped-favicon-32x32.jpg\" sizes=\"32x32\" />\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/cropped-favicon-192x192.jpg\" sizes=\"192x192\" />\n<link rel=\"ap