Q&#038;A with the Director Billy McGrath.</p>\n</div><br/>\n\t\t\t\t<p><strong>\n\t\t\t\t\tThu 24 September 2026\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</strong></p>\n\t\t\t\t<p>Doors: 7pm; Starts: 7.30pm</p>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"btn arrow-right white-arrow\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<a style='background: #00ADDA' href=\"https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/event/u2s-adam-claytons-ballroom-boom-film-screening-and-qa/\">Info & Tickets</a>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div><!-- event-bottom -->\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t</div><!-- project-post  -->\t\n\t\n\t\t<div class=\"project-post\">\n\t\t\t<a class=\"project-link\" href=\"https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/event/a-want-in-her-by-myrid-carten-film-screening/\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t  \t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"cf featured-image\" style=\"background-image:linear-gradient(rgba(0,0,0,0),rgba(0,0,0,0)), url('https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/A-WANT-IN-HER-MYRID-with-her-Mother.jpg'); background-size:cover;background-position:center center;\">\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"term-bg white-text'\" style=\"background:#00ADDA ;color: #fff;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span>Film</span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"project-bottom\">\n\t\t\t\t<h3>‘A Want In Her’ by Myrid Carten Film Screening</h3>\n\t\t\t\t<div><p>Donegal born video-artist, Myrid Carten&#8217;s haunting feature debut presents a complex and unflinchingly honest portrait of her relationship with her alcoholic mother.</p>\n</div><br/>\n\t\t\t\t<p><strong>\n\t\t\t\t\tWed 30 September 2026\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</strong></p>\n\t\t\t\t<p>Doors: 7pm; Starts: 7.30pm</p>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"btn arrow-right white-arrow\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<a style='background: #00ADDA' href=\"https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/event/a-want-in-her-by-myrid-carten-film-screening/\">Info & Tickets</a>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div><!-- event-bottom -->\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t</div><!-- project-post  -->\t\n\t\n\t\t<div class=\"project-post\">\n\t\t\t<a class=\"project-link\" href=\"https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/event/storm-an-irish-nigerian-family-story/\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t  \t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"cf featured-image\" style=\"background-image:linear-gradient(rgba(0,0,0,0),rgba(0,0,0,0)), url('https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Storm-man-lighting-cigarette.jpg'); background-size:cover;background-position:center center;\">\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"term-bg white-text'\" style=\"background:#ffbb00 ;color: #fff;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span>Storytelling</span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"project-bottom\">\n\t\t\t\t<h3>Storm: An Irish Nigerian Family Story</h3>\n\t\t\t\t<div><p>Poet and playwright Gabriel Gbadamosi and storyteller Nicholas Gbadamosi bring their brother’s remarkable life to the stage through storytelling, poetry, film and music – a moving exploration of family, memory and belonging.</p>\n</div><br/>\n\t\t\t\t<p><strong>\n\t\t\t\t\tThu 12 November 2026\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</strong></p>\n\t\t\t\t<p>Doors 7pm, Starts 7.30pm</p>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"btn arrow-right white-arrow\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<a style='background: #ffbb00' href=\"https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/event/storm-an-irish-nigerian-family-story/\">Info & Tickets</a>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div><!-- event-bottom -->\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t</div><!-- project-post  -->\t\n\t\n\t\t<div class=\"project-post\">\n\t\t\t<a class=\"project-link\" href=\"https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/event/all-our-yesterdays-uk-premiere-film-screening/\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t  \t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"cf featured-image\" style=\"background-image:linear-gradient(rgba(0,0,0,0),rgba(0,0,0,0)), url('https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/POSTER-all-our.-Yesterdays-.png'); background-size:cover;background-position:center center;\">\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"term-bg white-text'\" style=\"background:#00ADDA ;color: #fff;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span>Film</span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"project-bottom\">\n\t\t\t\t<h3>“All Our Yesterdays” UK Premiere Film Screening</h3>\n\t\t\t\t<div><p>“One town. Over two hundred and fifty years. Seventy million descendants.”</p>\n</div><br/>\n\t\t\t\t<p><strong>\n\t\t\t\t\tSun 22 November 2026\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</strong></p>\n\t\t\t\t<p>7pm Doors, 7:30pm Start</p>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"btn arrow-right white-arrow\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<a style='background: #00ADDA' href=\"https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/event/all-our-yesterdays-uk-premiere-film-screening/\">Info & Tickets</a>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div><!-- event-bottom -->\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t</div><!-- project-post  -->\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</div><!-- project-search-wrap -->\n\t\n</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div><!-- .entry-content -->\n\t\t\t\t</div><!-- #post-## -->\n\n\n\t\t\t</div><!-- #content -->\n\t\t</div><!-- #container -->\n\n\t</div><!-- #main -->\n</div><!-- #wrapper -->\n\n\n<div class=\"second-footer-wrap cf\">\n\t\n\n\t\t\t<div id=\"footer-widget-area\" role=\"complementary\" class=\"fadein\">\n\n\t\t\t\t<div id=\"first\" class=\"widget-area\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<ul class=\"xoxo\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<li id=\"text-2\" class=\"widget-container widget_text\">\t\t\t<div class=\"textwidget\"><p><a href=\"https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/whats-on/\">What’s On</a><br />\n<a href=\"https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/education/\">Education</a><br />\n<a href=\"https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/room-hire/\">Room Hire</a><br />\n<a href=\"https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/ab